# Kandev {version} — corresponding-source references

This Debian package repackages Kandev's upstream standard server bundle. The
package contains upstream binaries and notices, not source archives. These
version-pinned references identify the upstream source and build entrypoints;
they do not assert source closure or make a compliance determination.

## Upstream source

- Release tag: `{tag}`
- Bundle build commit reported by `remote-helpers.json`: `{commit}`
- Source tree: <https://github.com/kdlbs/kandev/tree/{tag}>
- Source archive: <https://github.com/kdlbs/kandev/archive/refs/tags/{tag}.tar.gz>

## Upstream build entrypoints

The backend bundle build is defined in the tagged `apps/backend/Makefile`.
Its `build-runtime` target builds Kandev, the native `agentctl`, and the remote
helpers; `build-agentctl-remote` names the helper build targets. Supporting
source and scripts are in the same tagged tree. This package uses the official
release assets rather than building them from source.
